0.20.228.824 D srv  log_server_r: request:  {"content": "In this calculation, the cost of goods available for sale is the sum of beginning inventory and net purchases.You then use this weighted-average figure to assign a cost to both ending inventory and the cost of goods sold.The net result of using weighted average costing is that the recorded amount of inventory on hand represents a value somewhere between the oldest and newest units purchased into stock.eighted average costing is commonly used in situations where: 1  Inventory items are so intermingled that it is impossible to assign a specific cost to an individual unit. ", "add_special": true}
